         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nWhen we leave home for a park, a school or a market, we usually come back later.\n\nEarlier, we learned to picture numbers growing along a road, always walking where the numbers increase. In this class, we learn how to walk back.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "eaf6bd4e-9f68-4945-ae49-1e4e46321975",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "eaf6bd4e-9f68-4945-ae49-1e4e46321975",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "3918f1d9-8d7f-439f-8f76-e5c4ef741b5e",
               "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
               "page": "https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Axis.html",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Remembering the Axes\n\nRemember the road we built with some numbers marked on it. We call this road an **axis**.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><svg width=\"450\" height=\"100\"  fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\"> <defs> <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"> <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" /></marker> </defs> <line x1=\"2\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"15\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <text x=\"0\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">0</text> <text x=\"40\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">1</text> <text x=\"80\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">2</text> <text x=\"120\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">3</text> <text x=\"160\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">4</text> <text x=\"200\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">5</text> <text x=\"240\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">6</text> <text x=\"280\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">7</text> <text x=\"320\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">8</text> <text x=\"360\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"1.5em\">9</text> <line x1=\"5\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"5\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" /> <line x1=\"45\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" /> <line x1=\"85\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"85\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" /> <line x1=\"125\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" /> <line x1=\"165\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" /> <line x1=\"205\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" /> <line x1=\"245\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"245\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" /> <line x1=\"285\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"285\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" /> <line x1=\"325\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"325\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" /> <line x1=\"365\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"365\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"3\" />  </svg></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Graphic 1: Representation of an axis with numbers. The numbers are placed below the line, and an arrow on the right end indicates the direction in which the numbers grow.</b></p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "c2dc5fb2-cd6a-4f9b-ac6f-9a7386dacc79",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "c2dc5fb2-cd6a-4f9b-ac6f-9a7386dacc79",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Walking Five Steps\n\nStarting at 0, five steps to the right require two calculations we already know:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "| Adding | Multiplying |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 5 | 5 × 1 = 5 |",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": true,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "*Table 1: Representation of the five steps using mathematics.*",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "02246a91-2cb8-4fcf-aa5c-9c678ce57e96",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "02246a91-2cb8-4fcf-aa5c-9c678ce57e96",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "nerd",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "ad7733f8-38ad-406f-abee-d259e45bf383",
               "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
               "page": "https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Subtraction.html",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2010",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### A New Operation\n\nWhen we walk away from a starting point, we need a way to measure that distance. We can already add or multiply the steps. Now we introduce **subtraction**, which measures the difference between two numbers.\n\nFor our 5 steps:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p style=\"text-align=center\"><center>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5<br />-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;0<br />____________<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5</center></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 1</b>: Number of steps from the origin.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "f5d92755-a0ce-4cef-9b98-e391041950fd",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "f5d92755-a0ce-4cef-9b98-e391041950fd",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Back to the Origin\n\nNow imagine we finish at our destination, 5 steps from the origin, and walk back the same number of steps. We reach the origin again — and we can show it with a subtraction:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p style=\"text-align=center\"><center>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5<br />-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5<br />____________<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;0</center></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 2</b>: Return to the origin.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "918c12d2-a14b-4686-abad-7d6b536e5668",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "918c12d2-a14b-4686-abad-7d6b536e5668",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "shocking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### From Another Starting Point\n\nNow suppose we start at position 1 and stop at position 9. To count the steps, subtract 1 from 9:",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p style=\"text-align=center\"><center>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;9<br />-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1<br />____________<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;8</center></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 3</b>: Number of steps between two positions.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "e1253c1d-a5bd-4e5e-82f1-66890737e4c2",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "e1253c1d-a5bd-4e5e-82f1-66890737e4c2",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Let Us Think!\n\nCan we read the minus sign as walking back along an axis?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "2487e133-e610-426f-aacb-695ee1c5d6c4",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "yes",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "2487e133-e610-426f-aacb-695ee1c5d6c4",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "nerd",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### A Signal to Return\n\nLook at the two subtractions we did (5 − 5 = 0 and 9 − 1 = 8). Each result is smaller than the value we started with, so we moved back along the axis.\n\nThat is why the minus sign (−) tells us to change direction, while the plus sign (+) in addition moves us forward on the same axis.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "6221f0f6-b47e-4d93-8138-2a243b2c3cc7",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "6221f0f6-b47e-4d93-8138-2a243b2c3cc7",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "party",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=964083ad-c587-43dc-9649-5b578714ab44",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this class, we learned about a new operation: **subtraction**. We use it to measure distances and lengths, and it can show a return to a previous position.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      }
   ]
}
